WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.833
In the previous two verses,

2
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:49.166
Lord Krishna shed light

3
00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:52.125
on the topics of sannyasa and yoga.

4
00:00:52.125 --> 00:00:56.250
Now in these third and fourth
verses of the sixth chapter,

5
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.750
Lord Krishna is explaining the stages of yoga.

6
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.750
In the third verse

7
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.458
of this chapter, Lord Krishna says

8
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:10.625
that on the path of yoga, there are two main

9
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:12.416
stages of practice –

10
00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:15.375
one for new practitioners and the other

11
00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.333
for practitioners

12
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:19.375
who have already made progress on this path.

13
00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:23.041
The initial stage is called "yogārurukșu."

14
00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:28.250
In this stage, a person should continue to 
fulfill their worldly duties,

15
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.375
because they have not yet

16
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:30.625
achieved that level of mental purification

17
00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:35.458
where they can completely renounce actions.

18
00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:38.875
Progressing on this path, eventually

19
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:40.083
a person attains "yogārūḍha,"

20
00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:44.208
meaning the advanced stage of yoga.

21
00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:45.041
In this stage,

22
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:48.291
a yogi's mind has become pure.

23
00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:50.541
Only upon reaching this advanced stage

24
00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:53.833
is renunciation of worldly actions appropriate.

25
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:56.458
In the initial stages of Ashtanga Yoga,

26
00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:57.708
a person's purpose is

27
00:01:57.708 --> 00:01:58.916
to control their behavior,

28
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:01.958
body, and mind.

29
00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:03.125
This practice

30
00:02:03.125 --> 00:02:05.375
can be done even while living among

31
00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.041
worldly duties.

32
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:08.791
Practicing these controls 
while remaining in the world

33
00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:10.583
brings that discipline in a person

34
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:12.541
which is essential

35
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:13.375
for the

36
00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:16.125
advanced stage of yoga.

37
00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:18.916
As a yogi progresses,

38
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:21.041
through this increasing discipline, they learn to

39
00:02:21.041 --> 00:02:24.083
avoid the wandering of the senses

40
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.583
and focus their attention

41
00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:27.916
within.

42
00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:30.291
And progressing on this path,

43
00:02:30.291 --> 00:02:31.250
that yogi

44
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.333
can eventually reach the highest stage,

45
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:36.875
beyond which is samadhi.

46
00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:39.583
That samadhi where the 
mind becomes completely

47
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:43.250
absorbed in meditation on God.

48
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.500
But a yogi can only reach

49
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.083
this stage

50
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.916
when they have practiced yoga

51
00:02:48.916 --> 00:02:50.416
and meditation while remaining

52
00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:53.416
amidst worldly duties.

53
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:56.416
This fact contradicts the notion

54
00:02:56.416 --> 00:02:58.166
that renouncing duties

55
00:02:58.166 --> 00:03:00.041
means progressing in yoga.

56
00:03:00.041 --> 00:03:02.791
Whereas the truth is that in the initial stage,

57
00:03:02.791 --> 00:03:06.625
practicing yoga amidst duties is essential.

58
00:03:06.625 --> 00:03:09.666
Now a natural question arises here:

59
00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:11.416
how will one know

60
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:13.875
that a person has reached from
 the initial stage to the advanced

61
00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:16.458
stage of yoga?

62
00:03:16.458 --> 00:03:18.625
The answer is in the fourth verse.

63
00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:20.041
Lord Krishna says

64
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:23.458
that a person is considered 
advanced on the path of yoga

65
00:03:23.458 --> 00:03:25.458
when they perform no duty

66
00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:28.208
for the satisfaction of the senses,

67
00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:28.875
nor do they

68
00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:32.875
desire to enjoy the fruits of their actions.

69
00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:34.166
Essentially, one who

70
00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:36.791
has renounced material desires

71
00:03:36.791 --> 00:03:39.041
is an advanced yogi.

72
00:03:39.041 --> 00:03:40.583
Understand its three parts:

73
00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:41.458
First –

74
00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:44.041
freedom from the desire for sensory pleasure –

75
00:03:44.041 --> 00:03:45.041
such a yogi

76
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:47.750
performs no action in the present for

77
00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:53.791
the enjoyment of taste, 
touch, sight, smell, and hearing.

78
00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:57.250
This craving has completely vanished in them.

79
00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.541
Second part –

80
00:03:58.541 --> 00:04:01.166
freedom from expectations
 of future happiness –

81
00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:03.291
such a yogi performs no action

82
00:04:03.291 --> 00:04:06.041
with expectations for the future either.

83
00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:07.875
Prosperity, wealth,

84
00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:09.583
honor, etc. –

85
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.666
they have risen above all of these.

86
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:15.208
Third part – renunciation of internal desires –

87
00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:16.333
such a yogi

88
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:18.041
has not only renounced the craving for external

89
00:04:18.041 --> 00:04:20.083
sensory pleasures,

90
00:04:20.083 --> 00:04:22.041
but these cravings no longer arise

91
00:04:22.041 --> 00:04:24.416
within their mind either.

92
00:04:24.416 --> 00:04:28.708
This state is called "sarva-sańkalpa-sannyāsī."

93
00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.541
It is important to understand these two verses,

94
00:04:31.541 --> 00:04:36.041
because many people make the mistake of 
thinking that renouncing duties

95
00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:38.041
means renouncing desires.

96
00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:40.416
Whereas desire is within a person.

97
00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:42.583
To eliminate this desire

98
00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:44.625
and to advance in yoga,

99
00:04:44.625 --> 00:04:47.125
while remaining amidst worldly duties,

100
00:04:47.125 --> 00:04:49.875
this desire must be eliminated.

101
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.291
People are often in a hurry,

102
00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:02.041
and it is natural that they 
will also want to progress

103
00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:06.875
on the path of yoga quickly, very quickly.

104
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:10.541
But it is essential to remember

105
00:05:10.541 --> 00:05:13.833
that this progress is only possible

106
00:05:13.833 --> 00:05:17.500
according to a systematic
 process of correct steps.

107
00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.291
If any step of this process is skipped,

108
00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:26.250
your efforts in yoga will become futile.

109
00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:29.833
All of life, all worldly duties,

110
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:35.041
are an extremely important
part of yoga practice.

111
00:05:35.041 --> 00:05:38.791
All these duties must be fulfilled.

112
00:05:38.791 --> 00:05:40.041
Renouncing these duties

113
00:05:40.041 --> 00:05:45.833
without reaching the advanced stage of yoga

114
00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:48.541
is a very big mistake.

115
00:05:48.541 --> 00:05:51.541
When you fulfill your duties, in the beginning

116
00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:54.833
there will be desires in the mind,

117
00:05:54.833 --> 00:05:57.125
there will be attachment to fruits.

118
00:05:57.125 --> 00:06:01.875
Don't renounce duties, but gradually renounce

119
00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:06.291
these internal desires while fulfilling duties.

120
00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:09.583
This is what will purify the mind.

121
00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:13.375
And this very purification will take you to that

122
00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:16.500
excellent stage of yoga

123
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.958
where renouncing duties also becomes possible.

124
00:06:21.958 --> 00:06:24.000
People often find

125
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
their duties burdensome,

126
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.333
they want freedom from them.

127
00:06:29.333 --> 00:06:34.416
But if those duties feel like a burden to you,

128
00:06:34.416 --> 00:06:36.458
it simply means

129
00:06:36.458 --> 00:06:40.750
you have a desire to get rid of the burden.

130
00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.541
And if there is desire,

131
00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:47.500
progress in yoga is still

132
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.666
far away.

133
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:53.208
Therefore, fulfill all your worldly duties,

134
00:06:53.208 --> 00:06:55.791
fulfill them with complete dedication.

135
00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:58.125
Only remove from your mind

136
00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:00.958
the desires related to these duties,

137
00:07:00.958 --> 00:07:06.250
or the expectations connected to them.

138
00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.583
Liberation will not come from

139
00:07:07.583 --> 00:07:10.125
external renunciation alone,

140
00:07:10.125 --> 00:07:13.958
you must also make changes from within.

141
00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:20.000
Everyone in a family

142
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.416
is different.

143
00:07:22.416 --> 00:07:23.541
Their thinking,

144
00:07:23.541 --> 00:07:27.041
their understanding, their way of living life –

145
00:07:27.041 --> 00:07:31.000
all are often different.

146
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.333
What interests one person

147
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:35.791
doesn't necessarily

148
00:07:35.791 --> 00:07:39.791
interest others in the same thing.

149
00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:41.875
Expecting the same type of behavior

150
00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:45.916
from everyone would be a mistake, wouldn't it?

151
00:07:45.916 --> 00:07:50.250
Because everyone is on their own life journey,

152
00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:52.791
everyone's circumstances are different,

153
00:07:52.791 --> 00:07:55.458
their definition of progress is different.

154
00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:57.958
Just look at yoga itself.

155
00:07:57.958 --> 00:08:01.375
For a person at the initial level of yoga,

156
00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:02.666
action itself is

157
00:08:02.666 --> 00:08:06.166
the means of spiritual progress.

158
00:08:06.166 --> 00:08:10.250
But for one who has advanced in yoga,

159
00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.791
for spiritual progress

160
00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:14.166
stopping the material activities of the senses

161
00:08:14.166 --> 00:08:17.125
will be appropriate.

162
00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:18.666
Therefore,

163
00:08:18.666 --> 00:08:20.875
if you are an elder in the family,

164
00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:24.125
remember this – what is appropriate

165
00:08:24.125 --> 00:08:27.833
for one person may be

166
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:31.083
inappropriate for another.

167
00:08:31.083 --> 00:08:34.416
If an attempt is made to impose the same rules

168
00:08:34.416 --> 00:08:36.791
on everyone,

169
00:08:36.791 --> 00:08:41.000
only tension and disagreement will arise.

170
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:46.333
This same thing must be remembered
when giving guidance to someone.

171
00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:49.208
For proper guidance, fully
 understanding a person's

172
00:08:49.208 --> 00:08:50.583
mental state

173
00:08:50.583 --> 00:08:54.083
is extremely important.

174
00:08:54.083 --> 00:08:55.916
Before giving anyone advice or instructions,

175
00:08:55.916 --> 00:08:59.375
understand their situation,

176
00:08:59.375 --> 00:09:00.791
listen to their thoughts,

177
00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:03.666
and respect those thoughts.

178
00:09:03.666 --> 00:09:05.083
By doing so, not only will you

179
00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:07.541
be able to give appropriate advice,

180
00:09:07.541 --> 00:09:11.125
but the other person will also

181
00:09:11.125 --> 00:09:15.125
understand and follow your advice with respect.

182
00:09:15.125 --> 00:09:18.416
And through this better
 understanding of each other,

183
00:09:18.416 --> 00:09:21.708
through respect for each other,

184
00:09:21.708 --> 00:09:25.166
love and trust in the family grow.

185
00:09:29.791 --> 00:09:31.333
From yoga

186
00:09:31.333 --> 00:09:34.500
and its path of progress,

187
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.458
many things about professional life

188
00:09:36.458 --> 00:09:39.958
can also be learned.

189
00:09:39.958 --> 00:09:42.583
For progress in yoga, it is necessary

190
00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:45.541
that a yogi fulfills all duties

191
00:09:45.541 --> 00:09:49.666
but stays away from personal 
selfishness and petty cravings.

192
00:09:49.666 --> 00:09:53.250
Also, their life must be inspired
 by the higher purposes

193
00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:57.833
of spirituality and human welfare.

194
00:09:57.833 --> 00:10:00.708
In exactly the same way,

195
00:10:00.708 --> 00:10:02.416
for higher leadership in an organization,

196
00:10:02.416 --> 00:10:04.333
that person will be suitable

197
00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.875
who stays away from petty selfishness,

198
00:10:06.875 --> 00:10:09.250
desires the progress of others,

199
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:13.208
and whose professional life is inspired by the higher

200
00:10:13.208 --> 00:10:17.333
purposes of organizational progress and 
contribution to society.

201
00:10:17.333 --> 00:10:18.541
Just as an advanced

202
00:10:18.541 --> 00:10:19.625
yogi's mind

203
00:10:19.625 --> 00:10:22.875
doesn't wander for the 
attainment of sensory pleasures,

204
00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:25.583
similarly, for a person appointed
 to a leadership position,

205
00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:28.166
it is essential that

206
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:31.791
no temptation can make them stray.

207
00:10:31.791 --> 00:10:34.416
Whether it be the temptation of money,

208
00:10:34.416 --> 00:10:37.083
position,

209
00:10:37.083 --> 00:10:40.083
or even physical attraction.

210
00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:42.833
You will find many examples

211
00:10:42.833 --> 00:10:47.708
where senior officials strayed due
 to temptations of money or lust

212
00:10:47.708 --> 00:10:51.250
and destroyed in an instant

213
00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:56.166
the honor they had earned over years.

214
00:10:56.166 --> 00:11:00.333
Avoiding such harmful temptations is essential.

215
00:11:00.333 --> 00:11:03.625
Just as an advanced yogi

216
00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:05.583
remains focused

217
00:11:05.583 --> 00:11:08.875
on the goal of meeting God, similarly,

218
00:11:08.875 --> 00:11:12.333
a senior official should remain focused
 on the organization's progress,

219
00:11:12.333 --> 00:11:13.958
society's advancement,

220
00:11:13.958 --> 00:11:18.750
and colleagues' growth.

221
00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.333
Excellent leadership is that

222
00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:26.500
which is desireless and selfless, like yoga.
